<!--
  Declared breaks against 1.0.0-beta.1.1, permitted by the repository's prerelease-stability policy and
  required by it to be declared. Three changes account for every entry here: the store implements the
  scoped, guarded, paged Docket contract (dropping the two unscoped expiry members the sweep used to
  call, and the unscoped amendments overwrite that had no caller left); MarkBlockedAsync takes the
  scope every other member that moves a row takes; and every component that needs the current instant
  takes an injectable TimeProvider as an added constructor parameter.

  A fourth: UpdateReviewStatusAsync is gone from the store — an entry id and a status, with no
  tenant scope, no expected status and no attestation check — superseded by the guarded
  TransitionAsync; and CountPendingAsync is added for the depth gauge.

  See CHANGELOG.md's upgrade notes.
-->
